{"cluster_id": "C-1442", "topic": "SensitivityCheckOrderingComparisonDiscriminates is not a valid sensitivity check", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["B046-017"], "canonical_claim": "SensitivityCheckOrderingComparisonDiscriminates is not a valid sensitivity check because EXPECT_FALSE(*body_index > *ckpt_index) duplicates the scenario and is weaker than test 1's EXPECT_LT(*body_index, *ckpt_index); the recorded mutation run is the meaningful evidence.", "issue_ids": ["F3"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t2-review.md#L146-L157"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1443", "topic": "ordinary `clickhouse-disks write` verb currently does not reach `blobUploadPool(", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["B049-070"], "canonical_claim": "The ordinary `clickhouse-disks write` verb currently does not reach `blobUploadPool()` because plain files use `CaInlineWriteBuffer` and part-shaped autocommit writes are `NOT_IMPLEMENTED`; pool initialization there is defense-in-depth for other or future non-autocommit paths.", "issue_ids": ["rev-s1-t5 Important"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/task-5-report.md#fix-round-1-rev-s1-t5-important"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1444", "topic": "`StorageReplicatedMergeTree", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["B051-100"], "canonical_claim": "The `StorageReplicatedMergeTree::checkAlterPartitionIsPossible` override that only delegates to the virtual base adds no behavior and should be deleted together with its header declaration.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/upstream-patch-inventory.md#storage-replicated-merge-tree"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1445", "topic": "EBR (Epoch-Based Reclamation) GC core -- writers holding a pin epoch (an ephemer", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M-024"], "canonical_claim": "An EBR (Epoch-Based Reclamation) GC core -- writers holding a pin epoch (an ephemeral Keeper node), GC advancing through safe_epoch/commit_epoch/birth_epoch and waiting for quiescence, with generations on blob keys (blobs/<H>/<g>) as the ABA guard -- was rejected because a stuck or wedged writer held down safe_epoch and stalled reclamation of all dropped parts across all writers, Keeper was required for correctness, and a long-running INSERT could delay GC for its entire duration. It was replaced by the incarnation-token design, where regular GC candidates are restricted to journal-known nodes so fresh uploads are structurally invisible and can never be candidates, and a wedged writer has no pin to hold down.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/01-architecture.md#rejected-ebr-gc"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1446", "topic": "Whole-object copy-on-write for `RefTableState", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M-067"], "canonical_claim": "Whole-object copy-on-write for `RefTableState::committed` via `src/Common/COW.h` (clone the whole map on any write) was rejected as \"approach C\" because trial copies during a flush always write, so it gives no gain over the naive full-map copy.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-17-cas-reftable-cow-map-design.md#L28"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1447", "topic": "Three fixes for the GC-registry monotone-growth problem were rejected before the", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-003"], "canonical_claim": "Three fixes for the GC-registry monotone-growth problem were rejected before the shard-incarnation redesign: (1) writer deregisters at `dropNamespace` \u2014 unsafe because the removal `-1` in-degree edges would be lost if the namespace vanished from discovery before GC folded that window; (2) GC hard-deregisters when 'empty + settled' \u2014 indistinguishable from a live table between CREATE and its first INSERT; (3) shard-object deletion on the path-keyed cursor \u2014 an ABA hazard where a recreated shard resets `shard_version` to 0 and an old sealed cursor silently skips the new incarnation's events.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/02-methodology.md#L169-L182"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1448", "topic": "Rejected writer-protocol designs", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-026"], "canonical_claim": "Rejected writer-protocol designs: `cas_owner` S3-metadata + `protectedByLiveBuild` guard (adopt did not transfer ownership, protection was revocable); a per-build heartbeat object at `builds/<build_id>` (leaked on successful publish, broke `DeletedCandidateDoesNotReappear`); `Build::resurrect` via GET-from-existing (raced GC delete in the HEAD-to-GET window); retaining full blob bodies in RAM (rejected on memory grounds for gigabyte column blobs); server-side copy/`UploadPartCopy` for bodyless re-stamp (dropped once the per-server watermark made bodyless re-stamp unnecessary; MinIO has known `UploadPartCopy` gaps); publish-at-precommit double-write (would add a second manifest PUT per part).", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/03-writer-protocol.md#L770-L786"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1449", "topic": "E4 (flat-vector base for RefTableState) was REVERTED after implementation", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-128"], "canonical_claim": "E4 (flat-vector base for RefTableState) was REVERTED after implementation: it only cleared Materialize's asymptotic cost 2x (O(NlogN)->O(N)) on a cost that is per-flush, never trace-visible, and N-budget-bounded, so simplicity won over the marginal gain.", "issue_ids": ["T6"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-21-unattended-reftablestate-experiments.md#timeline"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1450", "topic": "Keeping a permanent `Retired` catalog row instead of the transient `RemovalReady", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-335"], "canonical_claim": "Keeping a permanent `Retired` catalog row instead of the transient `RemovalReady` state was rejected because it grows the catalog with historical namespace births, eventually exhausts its object cap, and breaks supported exact-name reuse.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-31-task5-removalready-proposal.md#rejected-simpler-looking-alternatives"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1451", "topic": "Trusting only the historical pruned-seal observation (without a `RemovalReady` c", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-336"], "canonical_claim": "Trusting only the historical pruned-seal observation (without a `RemovalReady` catalog state) was rejected because another round can recreate the name-keyed cursor while the catalog entry remains `Removing`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-31-task5-removalready-proposal.md#rejected-simpler-looking-alternatives"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1452", "topic": "Keeping `_cleanup` as permanent removal evidence was rejected because a marker t", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-337"], "canonical_claim": "Keeping `_cleanup` as permanent removal evidence was rejected because a marker that must outlive every possibly stalled actor is unbounded, and deleting it recreates the stale-leader race it was introduced to prevent.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-31-task5-removalready-proposal.md#rejected-simpler-looking-alternatives"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1453", "topic": "Inferring damage from entry-less debris was rejected because legal debris and a ", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-338"], "canonical_claim": "Inferring damage from entry-less debris was rejected because legal debris and a fabricated missing catalog entry are physically indistinguishable; adding more classifier branches cannot create information that was never persisted.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-31-task5-removalready-proposal.md#rejected-simpler-looking-alternatives"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1454", "topic": "Life-scoped cursors were rejected as the primary Task 5 mechanism because they c", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-339"], "canonical_claim": "Life-scoped cursors were rejected as the primary Task 5 mechanism because they change the fold-seal wire grammar, every cursor key builder/parser, GC intake, REBUILD, fsck, and manifest sweep coverage lookup, while `RemovalReady` changes only one catalog enum, its codec, one transition, and the GC universe predicate.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-31-task5-removalready-proposal.md#comparison-with-life-scoped-cursors"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1455", "topic": "reviewer's objection that the `src/Common/ProfileEvents", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-390"], "canonical_claim": "A reviewer's objection that the `src/Common/ProfileEvents.cpp` registration exceeded the approved failpoint scope was refuted as a conflation: the registration came from a separate task, not the failpoint-approval task, and a `ProfileEvent` registration is not protocol coupling; the failpoint approval's actual scope (only `src/Common/FailPoint.cpp` registration lines) was exercised exactly as recorded.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-24-cas-publish-confirm-and-ref-lane-safety.md#L877-L881"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1456", "topic": "later draft of the relink/seam TLA+ model omitted FloorReconcile entirely while ", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-437"], "canonical_claim": "A later draft of the relink/seam TLA+ model omitted FloorReconcile entirely while leaving WedgeResolveInstall enabled on sWedge /\\ sApplyOwed, which admitted a poisoned-to-clean install as reachable when it should be impossible; a blanket ~sWedge exclusion in MarkerCoversDurableWindow was rejected because it hid the bug rather than describing the code \u2014 once the invariant's subject became the mount's own owed apply, no exclusion was needed for either the wedge or the fence.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-29-cas-relink-seam-tla-gate.md#L2106"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1457", "topic": "Five same-class defect hardening findings (H1-H5) followed the B85/B87 fixes", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-009"], "canonical_claim": "Five same-class defect hardening findings (H1-H5) followed the B85/B87 fixes: H1 four unchecked `resolvePartGenKeyForRead` call sites in `getLastModified` could wedge `clearOldTemporaryDirectories` on DROP; H2/H3 two sites threw `LOGICAL_ERROR` for benign concurrent DROP/DETACH races that should have thrown recoverable `FILE_DOESNT_EXIST`; H4 `replaceFile` lacked the `is_part_dir` directory delegation `moveFile` had just received; H5 `ContentAddressedGC::listLivePartIds` did a LIST-then-read without swallowing a concurrently-dropped ref.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/02-methodology.md#L295-L307"]}
