{"cluster_id": "C-1463", "topic": "ref-lease-exclusivity rev", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-392"], "canonical_claim": "The ref-lease-exclusivity rev.6 proposal left four open questions for review at draft time: whether a 30s `T_mat` unclean-handover penalty is acceptable in production given rustfs/MinIO/real-S3 request-lifetime differences; whether the eager recovery snapshot should also run on clean mounts with a large inherited tail; whether the seal's wedge/single-in-flight invariant may be hard-required via chassert plus release fail-close at the lane level; and confirming that the interim mechanical patch (aged trigger, copy-once replay, threshold 256) lands regardless of the proposal's outcome.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-13-cas-ref-lease-exclusivity-rev6-proposal.md#L151-L162"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1464", "topic": "generation handoff leak", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B001-016", "B001-048"], "canonical_claim": "The GC retention cursor can advance past a still-referenced generation before the best-effort hand-off or wholesale delete; if the process crashes after the retention cursor CAS and before deleting the `gc/gen/<g>/` prefix, a whole generation can leak until fsck, and a normal retry does not revisit the advanced cursor.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/00-REPORT.md#L545-L548", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/03-gc-refs.md#L475-L488"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1465", "topic": "pending manifest preservation", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B002-145", "B002-190", "B010-017", "B035-040"], "canonical_claim": "The orphan sweep must preserve or skip a dropped but unsealed committed manifest body with a pending removal because the removal fold still needs that body to emit its decrement; this was the condition shown by GC-WEDGE-2026-07-10.; A GC removal-fold wedge can clamp a shard forever when `CasOrphanManifestSweep` deletes a promoted manifest body after `dropRef` but before the committed-removal `-1` is sealed; the fold then cannot read the body to compute edge deltas and pool-wide graduation stops.; The committed-removal sweep must preserve a body after a `-1` removal is appended but before that removal is sealed by the GC fold, because the fold still needs the body to emit the decrement; the body becomes sweepable only after the removal is sealed.", "issue_ids": ["GC-WEDGE-2026-07-10"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/06-tla-models.md#camanifestsweepwindow", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-10-cas-meta-descriptor-raw-body.md#L76-L245", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/06-tests.md#3-regression-pin-archaeology-bug-ids-invariant-encoded", "utils/ca-soak/scenarios/BACKLOG.md#L1730-L1816"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1466", "topic": "abandoned precommit parked shard", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B002-181", "B007-067", "B007-070", "B035-029"], "canonical_claim": "The `SkipParksDeadPrecommit` model found that token-diff discovery could permanently park a static shard containing a watermark-dead abandoned precommit; the fix forces a read when the sealed coverage reports such a precommit.; The force-Read fix must preserve `Skip` for a shard with no live precommit or a live-but-not-yet-dead precommit, and must be idempotent after the removal changes the shard token.; The force-Read guard is self-terminating: reclaim appends a removal, the shard token changes, the next round reads normally, and the shard becomes `Skip`-eligible after coverage no longer contains a live precommit.; An abandoned precommit manifest could remain permanently protected when `CasOrphanManifestSweep` saw a `Precommit` binding with no removal event; a content-static shard parked by token-diff `Skip` prevented `reclaimAbandonedPrecommit` from running again.", "issue_ids": ["DANGLING-PRECOMMIT", "S30"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/06-tla-models.md#skipparksdeadprecommit", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-07-cas-dangling-precommit-manifest-orphan-fix.md#task-5", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-07-cas-dangling-precommit-manifest-orphan-fix-design.md#fix", "utils/ca-soak/scenarios/BACKLOG.md#L1251-L1287"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1467", "topic": "concurrent GC leader artifacts", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B001-046", "B002-019", "B002-044", "B003-086", "B011-029", "B035-003", "B035-004", "B035-006", "B038-081"], "canonical_claim": "A crashed GC pass leaves only unadopted attempt-scoped artifacts; there is no crash-resume step, and later pruning reclaims those artifacts.; Attempt-scoped GC artifacts are written under `gc/gen/<G_f>/attempt/<a>/` before adoption, and an unadopted attempt is invisible to readers.; A round uses `a = lease.seq` as its attempt identifier, so competing leaders write to distinct attempt prefixes and only the lease-token `gc/state` CAS can adopt one attempt.; Concurrent explicit GC leaders could orphan blobs because a deposed leader wrote a final-key fold seal before losing the `gc/state` CAS; attempt-scoped generations keyed by `(gen, attempt = lease.seq)` fix this by hiding unadopted artifacts.; A crash between run PUT and seal or state CAS leaves orphan attempt-scoped artifacts that retention prunes through `snap_pruned_through` under B174.; Concurrent explicit `SYSTEM CAS GC RUN ca` leaders could permanently orphan unreachable content blobs and part-manifests while preserving safety (`fsck dangling=0`); the leak occurred because an aborted divergent fold advanced generation or cursor state past owner-removal events that were never folded.; The concurrent-leader GC leak arose because `fold()` wrote `gc/gen/<gen>/fold_seal` before the lease-guarded `gc/state` CAS; a divergent `putIfAbsent` caused the losing leader to throw `ABORTED` without advancing state, so the winner's seal was never re-adopted and its owner-removal events were not re-folded.; Unadopted GC attempts are invisible to readers, resume, prune, and `RetireView`, so a deposed leader cannot collide on a final-key seal; unadopted attempt debris is reclaimed by wholesale `gc/gen/<g>/` retention pruning.; Every per-round GC artifact is keyed by `(gen, attempt = lease.seq)`, so artifacts from a deposed leader remain under an unadopted attempt.", "issue_ids": ["B174", "GC-CONCURRENT-LEADER-LEAK", "S33"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/04-gc-protocol.md#attempt-scoped-design", "docs/superpowers/cas/08-testing-and-soak.md#fixed", "docs/superpowers/cas/ROADMAP.md#area-gc", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/03-gc-refs.md#L334-L341", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-cas-retired-in-snapshot-design.md#adoption", "utils/ca-soak/scenarios/BACKLOG.md#L67-L74", "utils/ca-soak/scenarios/BACKLOG.md#L74-L74", "utils/ca-soak/scenarios/BACKLOG.md#L90-L95"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1468", "topic": "D1 originated because `dropNamespace` tombstoned shard contents but never remove", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B004-095"], "canonical_claim": "D1 originated because `dropNamespace` tombstoned shard contents but never removed the namespace from `gc/registry`, causing registry entries and empty ref-shard objects to accumulate as the S30 `other` residual.", "issue_ids": ["D1", "S05", "S30"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-01-cas-shard-incarnation-and-registry-removal-design.md#problem"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1469", "topic": "GC rebuild initially missed physical blobs with zero rebuilt edges because they ", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B006-055"], "canonical_claim": "GC rebuild initially missed physical blobs with zero rebuilt edges because they had no run row and never transitioned to zero; the rebuild now condemns such blobs directly using head-captured tokens, a minted round, and floor-gated graduation.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-03-unattended-night.md#L54-L60"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1470", "topic": "GC safety bug allowed clamped shards to skip landed events", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-181", "AUDIT-M2-322", "B006-058", "B037-106", "B038-090", "B044-016"], "canonical_claim": "A GC safety bug allowed clamped shards to skip landed events: a blob was deleted while its landed `+1` remained unfolded, yielding 31 dangling blobs and one dangling manifest; this violated INV-NO-LOSS.; A persistent clamp on one GC shard leaves `suppress_destructive` set for every pass and halts blob and manifest deletion and all GC reclamation across the entire pool, not just for the affected shard; the fail-closed behavior is retained, with recommended observability and an operator escape including clamp age, clamped key/shard, alerting, and a documented fsck/rebuild path, while scoped suppression is deferred.; CLAMP-SUPPRESSION was the 2026-07-03 night-soak bug where 31 dangling objects accumulated because a clamped fold cursor suppressed graduations and deletes pool-wide even though only one table was lagging.; A GC round that held back an unreadable shard must make no destructive decision, and the clamp-suppression guard prevents physical deletion while an unfolded delta could still touch the blob. Additionally, When any shard is clamped, GC performs no graduation and no pending deletes; a clamp-free pass resumes deletes and emits a `gc_fold_clamp` event.", "issue_ids": ["CLAMP-SUPPRESSION", "G-N1"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/ROADMAP.md#area-gc", "docs/superpowers/models/README.md#group-gc-core", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/06-tests.md#3-regression-pin-archaeology-bug-ids-invariant-encoded", "docs/superpowers/reports/reviews.md#L1492-L1493", "docs/superpowers/reports/reviews.md#L340-L351", "docs/superpowers/reports/reviews.md#L745-L745", "docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-03-unattended-night.md#L69-L79"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1471", "topic": "P2 reported 116 `delete_pending blob recovered in-degree \u2014 structurally impossib", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B007-019"], "canonical_claim": "P2 reported 116 `delete_pending blob recovered in-degree \u2014 structurally impossible under the ack floor (spared anyway, fail-closed)` events in a four-minute window on ch1; the root cause was unknown in the campaign.", "issue_ids": ["P2"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-06-cas-night-findings-fix-plan-design.md#re-audit"]}

